# ScriptedController.ChooseTargets (control.go) never validates its queued
# answer against the candidates it was offered, unlike a real player's UI or
# the AI -- this scenario uses that to isolate the CR 608.2b re-check
# (targetStillLegal -> cardCantBeTargetedBy) on its own, a target Java could
# never actually have chosen. TestTargetCandidates* (staticability_internal_test.go)
# holds the choice-time filter (targetCandidates) to the same rule directly.
# CR 702.16e: Protection's targeting half carries no Activator$ gate either
# (CardFactoryUtil.java's own Protection branch, ValidSource$ only) --
# matched against the spell's own color, not who casts it. human's red
# Lightning Bolt at ai's Narwhal (Protection from red) is still a legal
# candidate at cast time (ai remains a legal ValidTgts$ Any candidate too),
# but the CR 608.2b re-check finds Narwhal illegal against ValidSource$
# Card.Red and drops it -- Bolt fizzles, dealing no damage.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 1 R
queue targets 3
queue action human cast 2
passpriority
